Z||000000||carpetviper||12-08-2001||04:58 PM||||There is some paint on some areas like the hood ornament and the front parking lights that have black paint overspray on them from the previous owners home job. How can I remove this without having to buy the new pieces. Also there is some on the sunroof, can I just scrap this off?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Mach10||12-08-2001||05:10 PM||||Best bet is a rubbing/polishing compound. Get one that's safe for clear-coats (otherwise the chemicals turn 'em milky). Slap some one, and scrub with a nice soft CLEAN cloth  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||rogergarrison||12-08-2001||06:12 PM||||clay bar||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||12-08-2001||07:27 PM||||On the glass, use an SOS or Brillo pad with plenty of water. This will also work on lenses but will require you to polish them afterwards.||||reg||1
Z||000004||carpetviper||12-08-2001||11:54 PM||||So rubbing compound will work to get the paint off without damaging the hood emblem?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Good, I think I have some in the shed, hopefully its okay for clearcoat.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpetviper.gif"> ||||reg||1
